<title>JAPAN: Japan Apr oil product imports down 7.9 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Apr oil product imports down 7.9 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of International Trade and Industry issued the following data on oil product imports during April(barrel equivalents are also shown):</p>
<p>	 (In 1,000 kl)(1,000 bbl) mth/mth%  yr/yr %</p>
<p> Gasoline     102	  642    +96.2	-6.4</p>
<p> Naphtha    2,380     14,970     -5.6	+6.6</p>
<p> Kerosene	93	  585    -70.8     -54.6</p>
<p> Gas oil	 51	  321    -45.7     -83.3</p>
<p> Fuel oil A    80	  503    -11.1     -11.1</p>
<p> Fuel oil C   179	1,126     -0.6	-4.8</p>
<p> Total	2,885     18,147    -11.4	-7.9</p>
<p>(Note: LSWR imports are included in the Fuel oil C statistics)</p>
</text>
